---
alwaysApply: true
---

project:
  name: "AppsRow PM"
  description: "In-house project management tool for a Webflow agency. Minimal, schema-driven, role-based, and AI-friendly."
  techTarget:
    - "React/Next"
    - "TypeScript"
    - "TanStack Query (React Query)"
    - "Zustand or lightweight global store"
    - "Postgres/Supabase API"
  designTokens:
    primary: "#E90E1D"
    secondary: "#E7E7E7"
    surface: "#FFFFFF"
    radius: 14
    spacing: 8
    font: "Inter"

rules:
  # 1. STRUCTURE / ARCH
  - id: structure.feature-first
    description: "Organize code by feature/domain, not by component type."
    applyTo:
      - "src/features/*"
      - "src/services/*"
      - "src/shared/*"
    details:
      - "Each feature gets its own folder: tasks, projects, worklogs, users, reports, calendar."
      - "UI that belongs only to a feature lives inside that feature: src/features/worklogs/ui, src/features/calendar/ui."
      - "Shared UI/primitives go to src/shared/ui."
      - "Do not create giant pages that mix 3+ domains in one file. Split."

  - id: structure.file-size
    description: "Avoid god components."
    details:
      - "Any React component over 150–180 LOC must be split into smaller components."
      - "Calendar screens must split into: header, grid, day-details, dialogs."
      - "If a file mixes data-fetching, domain logic, and multiple dialogs → split."

  # 2. STATE LAYERS
  - id: state.split
    description: "Separate server-state and UI-state."
    details:
      - "Use React Query for server data (tasks, projects, worklogs, users, calendar entries)."
      - "Use local/component state for UI (modals, filters, tabs, selected date)."
      - "Use Zustand/Redux only for cross-page state (auth user, current role, sidebar, theme)."
      - "Do not duplicate server data in Zustand if React Query already caches it."

  - id: state.role-aware
    description: "UI must react to user role."
    details:
      - "Read current user from auth/Zustand context."
      - "If user.role == 'sales' → hide/disable create/edit worklogs in all views."
      - "If user.role == 'admin' → show admin layout + admin sidebar."
      - "Do not render restricted actions even if the API will reject them."

  # 3. DATA ACCESS / SERVICES
  - id: api.single-client
    description: "Use a single API/Supabase client for all HTTP/DB calls."
    details:
      - "Create src/services/apiClient.ts (or src/services/supabaseClient.ts) with base client and auth headers."
      - "Feature services (tasks, projects, worklogs, calendar) must import this client."
      - "Components must NOT call Supabase directly; they must call feature services."
      - "Service functions return data or throw. Do not show toasts in services."

  - id: api.versioned
    description: "All endpoints must be versioned for future expansion."
    details:
      - "Use /api/v1/... routes for current implementation."
      - "Do not call unversioned routes in production code."
      - "If Supabase RPC is used, wrap it in a versioned service function."

  - id: services.feature-based
    description: "Each domain gets a service file."
    details:
      - "src/features/worklogs/services/worklogService.ts → list, create, update, delete, check-duplicate."
      - "src/features/tasks/services/taskService.ts → list, updateStatus, listByProject."
      - "src/features/projects/services/projectService.ts → list, userProjects, counts."
      - "UI imports these services through React Query hooks, not directly."

  # 4. QUERIES / MUTATIONS
  - id: queries.scoped
    description: "All queries must be scoped to current user or context."
    details:
      - "Key queries by entity and filters: ['worklogs', { userId, month }], ['tasks', { userId, category }]."
      - "When user is logged in, always send userId in the query."
      - "Admin views may drop userId but must explicitly request it."

  - id: mutations.invalidate-targeted
    description: "After a mutation, invalidate only the affected queries."
    details:
      - "On add worklog: invalidate ['worklogs', { userId }], ['calendar', { userId }]."
      - "On edit/delete worklog: same as above."
      - "On task status change: invalidate ['tasks', { userId }], and ['projects', { userId }] if project counts depend on tasks."
      - "Do NOT invalidate '*' or unrelated keys."

  # 5. DOMAIN RULES (TASKS / WORKLOGS)
  - id: schema.respect
    description: "Respect DB schema in UI and services."
    details:
      - "Source of truth tables: users, projects, tasks, work_logs, status_history."
      - "tasks.category must be one of ['design','development']."
      - "Never invent fields not present in schema unless mapped in a DTO."
      - "When adding a worklog, user_id and task_id must come from authenticated context."

  - id: tasks.category-filter
    description: "Show only relevant tasks to the user based on department/specialization."
    details:
      - "If current_user.specialization or department contains 'design' → filter tasks.category = 'design'."
      - "If current_user.specialization or department contains 'dev' or 'development' → filter tasks.category = 'development'."
      - "If current_user.role == 'admin' → do not filter by category."
      - "If current_user.role == 'sales' → allow read-only access to tasks/projects but hide worklog creation."
      - "Apply this rule in: Assigned Tasks, Worklog Form (task select), Calendar, Worklog History."

  - id: events.audit
    description: "Task/project status changes must write to status_history."
    details:
      - "On task status update, insert into status_history { entity_type: 'task', entity_id, status, updated_by }."
      - "On project status update, same shape with entity_type: 'project'."
      - "Put this in the service layer, not inside the React component."
      - "UI should call a single service method like updateTaskWithHistory(...)."

  - id: worklogs.dup-guard
    description: "Guard against duplicate worklogs."
    details:
      - "Before creating: check existing worklog for (user_id, task_id, date, hours)."
      - "If match → show confirm modal."
      - "Keep this logic in a shared util so UI + service can reuse."
      - "Do not duplicate this logic in multiple components."

  # 6. UI / UX
  - id: ui.tokens
    description: "Use design tokens for colors, spacing, and radius."
    details:
      - "Primary color: #E90E1D."
      - "Secondary/surfaces: #E7E7E7."
      - "Radius: 14px, Spacing scale: 8px."
      - "No hard-coded colors in feature components; import from theme/tokens."
      - "If using shadcn, wrap it to inject tokens."

  - id: ui.modals-named
    description: "Modals and drawers must be named and reusable."
    details:
      - "Use ids/names like MdEditWorklog, DlDayDetails, DrTaskDetails."
      - "Do not create anonymous inline modals inside large components."
      - "Put shared modals in src/shared/modals."
      - "Calendar day details drawer must be a separate component."

  - id: ui.tables
    description: "All tables must be usable on desktop."
    details:
      - "Sticky header, sortable, filterable."
      - "Page size 20–25 by default."
      - "Empty state with CTA (e.g. 'Add Worklog')."

  - id: ux.loading-error-empty
    description: "Every data view must handle loading, error, and empty state."
    details:
      - "Loading: skeleton or spinner."
      - "Error: retry button, generic message."
      - "Empty: icon + CTA."
      - "Do NOT render a blank screen."

  - id: ui.calendar
    description: "Calendar view must stay thin."
    details:
      - "Calendar root component should only orchestrate: navigation, selected date, and data hooks."
      - "Day-details sheet/drawer must be separate."
      - "Add/Edit worklog dialogs must be separate components imported by calendar."
      - "No direct Supabase calls in the calendar component."

  # 7. PERFORMANCE
  - id: perf.pagination
    description: "Paginate large lists and debounce searches."
    details:
      - "Paginate lists > 50 rows."
      - "Debounce text search (300–400ms)."
      - "Prefer server-side filtering to client-side."

  # 8. VALIDATION
  - id: validation.double
    description: "Validate on client and server."
    details:
      - "Use Zod/Yup schemas in src/core/schemas/ for forms."
      - "Backend must re-validate required fields and enums."
      - "Worklog hours must be > 0 on both sides."
      - "Calendar add-worklog dialog must not submit empty task/project."

  # 9. CLEAN CODE
  - id: code.clean
    description: "Code must be readable and consistent."
    details:
      - "Use ESLint + Prettier."
      - "No console.log in production code; use a logger util if needed."
      - "Break components >150 lines into smaller ones."
      - "Use TypeScript types for API responses and React Query keys."

  # 10. DOCS / CONTEXT
  - id: docs.cursor-context
    description: "Keep a single source of context for AI/Cursor."
    details:
      - "Create /docs/cursor-context.md with schema, design tokens, routes, and Stitch rules."
      - "When generating new screens, reference that doc instead of re-describing everything."
      - "Update this doc when DB schema changes (like tasks.category)."
